# Trivy suppressions for the image scans in .github/workflows/docker-publish.yml.
#
# All three scans are blocking: a fixable HIGH/CRITICAL stops the publish before the image
# reaches GHCR. This file is the escape hatch when a release cannot wait for an upstream
# base-image rebuild - use it instead of re-adding `continue-on-error`, which silences every
# finding forever rather than one finding until a date.
#
# Format: one CVE per line, each with an expiry and a reason.
#
#   CVE-2026-12345 exp:2026-09-30  # <image>: <why we accept it> - tracked in #<issue>
#
# Rules:
# - Always set `exp:`. An entry without one never comes back for review.
# - Keep the window short (a few weeks). The expiry is a promise to revisit, not a deletion.
# - Say which image and why. "Not reachable from our code" is a claim someone must be able
#   to re-check when the entry expires.
#
# Unfixed CVEs do not belong here: `ignore-unfixed: true` already excludes them.

# --- api-web: compiled into the FrankenPHP binary, not reachable from our runtime ---
#
# Both live in Go modules linked into /usr/local/bin/frankenphp. We do not build that binary,
# so the only real fix is an upstream release, and 1.12.7 (2026-08-07) is the latest one.
# Tracked in #518; revisit when FrankenPHP ships a build with the bumped modules.
#
# kin-openapi: fail-open auth bypass in ValidationHandler.Load(). That handler is FrankenPHP's
# optional OpenAPI request validation - we do not enable it, Symfony does our routing and auth.
GHSA-r277-6w6q-xmqw exp:2026-10-01  # api-web: getkin/kin-openapi v0.140.0, ValidationHandler unused - #518
#
# grpc: xDS RBAC and HTTP/2 issues. We run FrankenPHP standalone behind Traefik, with no xDS
# control plane and no gRPC listener.
GHSA-hrxh-6v49-42gf exp:2026-10-01  # api-web: google.golang.org/grpc v1.81.1, no xDS/gRPC in use - #518
#
# Deux advisories de plus sur le même module, apparues le 2026-08-24 et bloquant la publication de
# la v0.16.4. Toutes deux sont dans `openapi3filter`, le validateur de requêtes OpenAPI de
# FrankenPHP : le déni de service par corps multipart malformé n'est atteignable que si
# l'application valide un corps de requête avec `ValidationErrorEncoder`/`ConvertErrors`, et
# l'explosion mémoire que si une spec déclare un paramètre `deepObject`. Nous n'embarquons aucun
# Caddyfile : l'image tourne sur celui livré par FrankenPHP, qui n'active pas cette validation, et
# c'est Symfony qui route et valide. FrankenPHP 1.12.7 (2026-08-07) reste sa dernière version, donc
# aucun correctif amont n'existe à ce jour.
CVE-2026-76905 exp:2026-10-01  # api-web: kin-openapi openapi3filter, validation OpenAPI non activée - #518
CVE-2026-77354 exp:2026-10-01  # api-web: kin-openapi openapi3filter, validation OpenAPI non activée - #518
